  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Exploring the Distributed Ledger Technology for Humanitarian Action in Malawi</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Unblocked Cash transfer system will be developed for vulnerable people who have been adversely affected by drought and further aggravated by COVID -19. Oxfam will use the Unblocked Cash transfer system for beneficiaries to collect food at selected local shops. Beneficiary House Holds (HH) will receive messages of transfers into their selected mobile platforms every month.  Beneficiaries will collect/withdraw cash/vouchers and redeem for food items at designated local shops and sign off to acknowledge redemption of the vouchers.  Due diligence for selected retailers will be done and communities will be educated on the voucher process and how to redeem and guard against theft. Oxfam and its Partner will set up a complaints mechanism in the event of any challenges. The E -voucher will empower communities to and prioritize the basic food commodities they prefer at household level.</narrative>
  </description>
